mixin () {
  /// Return the backend's public API documentation as Markdown.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Farm Tracking Backend API\n\nThis canister stores each farmer's profile, farm plots, and field activity log.\nAll data is private to the principal that created it: every read and write is\nscoped to the caller, and no endpoint accepts another farmer's principal.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\nEvery method below is a `shared` function that reads the caller's principal from\nthe message. There is no anonymous access: a caller that is not signed in with\nInternet Identity arrives as the anonymous principal, which owns no data, so\n`getProfile` returns `null`, `listPlots` returns `[]`, and every mutation\ncreates rows under that anonymous principal (they are unreachable once the\nsession ends).\n\nThe frontend pins an Internet Identity **derivation origin**, published at\n`/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin`. An agent that already holds the user's\nInternet Identity authorization must derive the per-app principal against that\norigin, for example:\n\n```\nicp identity link web <name> --app <host>\n```\n\nA principal derived against a different origin is a **different principal** and\nwill not see the data the app's frontend created. Such a delegation acts with\nthe user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\nThere is no registration step and no role system: the first call from a\nprincipal simply creates its own rows. There are no admin-only endpoints.\n\n## Authorization model\n\n- `getProfile` / `setProfile` operate on the caller's own profile only.\n- `listPlots` / `getPlot` / `addPlot` / `updatePlot` / `deletePlot` operate on\n  the caller's own plots only. `getPlot` returns `null` for a plot that exists\n  but belongs to someone else, so ownership is not leaked.\n- `listActivities` / `addActivity` operate on the caller's own activities only.\n  `addActivity` traps with `plot not found` when the target plot is not the\n  caller's.\n- `getDashboardSummary` summarizes the caller's own plots and activities.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- `Timestamp` is `Int`, **nanoseconds since the Unix epoch** (`Time.now()`).\n  Divide by 1_000_000_000 for seconds.\n- `PlotId` and `ActivityId` are `Nat`, assigned by the canister and unique\n  across all farmers (a single shared counter, not per-farmer).\n- `areaHectares`, `latitude`, `longitude` are `Float`. Latitude is in\n  `[-90, 90]`, longitude in `[-180, 180]`.\n- `ActivityType` is a variant: `#planting`, `#irrigation`, `#fertilizing`,\n  `#pestControl`, `#harvest`.\n- `locationLabel` is a free-text human label for the map pin; the coordinates\n  are the authoritative location. Weather is fetched by the frontend, not by\n  this canister.\n\n## Methods\n\n### `getProfile() : async ?FarmerProfile` (query)\nReturns `{ displayName : Text; defaultRegion : Text }` for the caller, or\n`null` when no profile has been saved.\n\n### `setProfile(displayName : Text, defaultRegion : Text) : async FarmerProfile` (update)\nCreates or **replaces** the caller's profile. Idempotent: calling it twice with\nthe same arguments leaves the same state.\n\n### `listPlots() : async [FarmPlot]` (query)\nReturns all of the caller's plots. Order is insertion order, not sorted.\n\n### `getPlot(plotId : PlotId) : async ?FarmPlot` (query)\nReturns the caller's plot with that id, or `null` if it does not exist or is\nnot the caller's.\n\n### `addPlot(input : FarmPlotInput) : async FarmPlot` (update)\nCreates a plot owned by the caller and returns it with its assigned `id` and\ntimestamps. `input` is\n`{ name; cropType; areaHectares; latitude; longitude; locationLabel }`.\nTraps on invalid input: blank `name`, `areaHectares <= 0`, latitude outside\n`[-90, 90]`, or longitude outside `[-180, 180]`. **Not idempotent** — each call\ncreates a new plot with a new id.\n\n### `updatePlot(plotId : PlotId, input : FarmPlotUpdate) : async FarmPlot` (update)\nReplaces the mutable fields of the caller's plot (same fields and validation as\n`addPlot`), preserving `id` and `createdAt` and refreshing `updatedAt`. Traps\nwith `plot not found` when the plot is not the caller's. Idempotent for the\nsame arguments.\n\n### `deletePlot(plotId : PlotId) : async Bool` (update)\nDeletes the caller's plot **and all activities logged against it**. Returns\n`true` when a plot was removed, `false` when no such plot belonged to the\ncaller. Destructive and **not idempotent in effect**: a second call returns\n`false` and the activities are already gone. The frontend asks for confirmation\nbefore calling this.\n\n### `listActivities(plotId : PlotId, filter : ?ActivityType) : async [FieldActivity]` (query)\nReturns the caller's activities for that plot, **newest first** by `date`.\nPass `null` for `filter` to get all types, or a variant such as `?#harvest` to\nrestrict to one type. Returns `[]` for a plot that is not the caller's.\n\n### `addActivity(input : FieldActivityInput) : async FieldActivity` (update)\nLogs an activity against one of the caller's plots. `input` is\n`{ plotId; activityType; date; notes }`. Traps with `plot not found` when the\nplot is not the caller's. `date` is caller-supplied and is not validated\nagainst the current time. **Not idempotent** — each call creates a new activity\nwith a new id.\n\n### `getDashboardSummary() : async DashboardSummary` (query)\nReturns `{ totalFarms : Nat; totalAreaHectares : Float; mostRecentActivity :\n?FieldActivity }` for the caller. `totalFarms` counts the caller's plots,\n`totalAreaHectares` sums their area, and `mostRecentActivity` is the caller's\nactivity with the greatest `date` across all of their plots, or `null` when\nnone exists.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\nAll methods are single-message calls with no background jobs, no async\ncompletion, and no server-side progress state. A mutation is complete when the\ncall resolves; there is nothing to poll. After a successful mutation the\nfrontend should re-read with the corresponding query (`listPlots`,\n`listActivities`, `getDashboardSummary`) rather than assume cached state.\n\n## Errors and limits\n\n- Validation failures and missing-plot failures are **traps**, which surface to\n  the caller as a rejected call with the message text (`name must not be\n  empty`, `areaHectares must be greater than zero`, `latitude must be between\n  -90 and 90`, `longitude must be between -180 and 180`, `plot not found`).\n  They are not typed error variants.\n- Queries (`getProfile`, `listPlots`, `getPlot`, `listActivities`,\n  `getDashboardSummary`, `getApiDoc`) never trap on missing data; they return\n  `null` or `[]`.\n- There is no pagination. `listPlots` and `listActivities` return the caller's\n  full result set, so a farmer with very many plots or activities receives them\n  all in one response.\n\n## Non-obvious gotchas\n\n- `getPlot` returning `null` is ambiguous between 'does not exist' and 'belongs\n  to another farmer' — by design, to avoid leaking ownership.\n- `deletePlot` cascades to activities; there is no way to delete a plot while\n  keeping its activity history.\n- `addPlot` and `addActivity` are not idempotent. Retrying a call that may have\n  succeeded creates a duplicate row; re-read first when a call's outcome is\n  uncertain.\n- `setProfile` and `updatePlot` are full replacements, not partial patches:\n  omitted fields are not preserved, they are overwritten with the supplied\n  values.\n- Ids are globally unique, so an id from one farmer's data never collides with\n  another's, but ids are not contiguous per farmer.\n";
  };
};
